/* DO NOT EDIT - machine generated by tools/generate/generate.py
 * source: ch32-riscv-ug/ch32-device-data tables, pinned in vendor/ch32-device-data.lock.toml
 *
 * CH32X033 pin map: the union of all 1 part numbers in the
 * series, so the same header serves the ANY menu entry and every SKU.
 *
 * Pin numbers are port-encoded (ADR-0010): pin = ((port + 2) << 5) | bit,
 * so PA0 is 64; 0..63 are left for a product board's printed numbers.
 * Every pin number is below NUM_DIGITAL_PINS, but the valid set is
 * SPARSE: 0..NUM_DIGITAL_PINS-1 has gaps, so test with
 * digitalPinIsValid(pin). CH32RV_GPIO_COUNT is the number of pads.
 *
 * A pad missing from a given package is left unbonded: writing it only
 * touches a register bit with nothing attached, which is harmless.
 *
 * Exception, errata x035-pc10-pc17-bonded: PC10/PC17 and PC11/PC16 are
 * internally bonded pairs sharing one lead; never drive both halves of a
 * pair. The core marks PC10/PC11 as the never-driven side.
 *
 * Behaviour, errata x035-usb-pads-open-drain: PC16/PC17 are the USB PHY
 * pads; while AFIO_CTLR.USB_PHY_V33 is set (reset default) an open-drain
 * output on them drives high instead of releasing. The core clears the bit
 * whenever either pad becomes an output (ch32rv_gpio_set_config); USB init
 * sets it again.
 *
 * Behaviour, errata x035-no-gpio-open-drain: The GPIO block has no
 * general-purpose open-drain output. OUTPUT_OPENDRAIN is emulated:
 * released is a floating input, low is push-pull low, and digitalWrite()
 * switches between them (wiring_digital.c).
 */
